1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[Uvogin] You tell the boss…

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
I’m not leaving.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,000
I can’t go back

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
until I settle the score
with that damn chain user!

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
[theme song playing]

6
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,000
CHASING x AND x WAITING

7
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
[narrator] Hisoka,
who joined the Phantom Troupe,

8
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
for a chance to fight the leader, Chrollo,

9
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,000
has proposed a partnership with Kurapika,

10
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
who is seeking revenge on the group.

11
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
[Hisoka] What are you going to do?

12
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Will you work with me?

13
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Or would you rather…

14
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
fight alone?

15
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
[phone ringing]

16
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Go ahead.

17
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Yes, it’s me.

18
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,000
[Melody] Terrible news.

19
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
The big man we captured has escaped.

20
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Escaped? All on his own?

21
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,000
[Melody] No.

22
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Some Phantom Troupe members
disguised themselves as Mafia henchmen

23
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
and came for him.

24
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,000
[Kurapika] And our leader?

25
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Not sure.

26
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,000
We haven’t been able to reach him.

27
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,000
[gasps]

28
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
[Melody] We’re moving to plan B.

29
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Get back here as soon as possible.

30
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Understood.

31
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
[Kurapika] Hisoka,
I have a question for you.

32
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Where can I find the Scarlet Eyes?

33
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
[Hisoka] Unfortunately,
that happened before I joined.

34
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,000
The Boss sells every item
after reveling in the spoils for a bit.

35
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
I assume the Scarlet Eyes
were no exception.

36
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
And that’s all
I can tell you on the matter.

37
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
But keep this in mind:

38
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
A spider will keep going
until you crush its head.

39
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
I suggested we form an alliance,

40
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
but not that we fight side by side.

41
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Merely the give and take
of certain information.

42
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
And if it ceases to benefit us,

43
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
there is no further obligation
to cooperate.

44
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Simple enough?

45
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
What do you say?

46
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
[Kurapika] I’ll be back here
at the same time tomorrow.

47
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
So? What do we do now?

48
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Our leader’s probably dead already.

49
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
And we still
haven’t completed the mission…

50
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
We should report this to the boss,
don’t you think?

51
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,000
That little girl is our boss in name only.

52
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,000
[Squala] Yeah, it was somebody else
who hired us.

53
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Light Nostrade.

54
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Her father.

55
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Our orders come directly from him.

56
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
The leader just relayed them to us.

57
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
And he was the only one
who knew how to contact him.

58
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,000
We have no choice.

59
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
We have to report this to the boss.

60
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Boss... Boss.

61
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,000
[stirring groan]

62
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
[Neon] Hold on, what time is it?

63
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
[Kurapika] It’s two in the morning.

64
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,000
[gasps in shock]

65
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Oh, no! What about the auction?!

66
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,000
[Kurapika] It's been called off.

67
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Huh?

68
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Completely? Why? What for?

69
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,000
There was a gang of thieves
who attacked the auction hall.

70
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Huh?

71
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:49,000
[Kurapika] Baise, Ivlenkov, and Tocino
lost their lives in the incident.

72
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Huh?

73
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
[Squala] We can’t reach the leader,
so he might also be…

74
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,000
No way…

75
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
But what about the mummy?

76
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Was it really stolen?

77
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
I wanted it so much…

78
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
-[Kurapika exhales]
-[Squala grunts]

79
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Seems the Mafia moved the merchandise
to a safe location.

80
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
[light giggle] That's great!
When’s the next one?

81
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
There’s another auction soon, right?

82
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,000
[Kurapika] We don't know yet.

83
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
You don’t? But why not?

84
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
In any case,

85
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
the leader handled all communication
with your father.

86
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
So, I’m afraid we don’t know anything.

87
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,000
And we can’t act
until we’ve received his orders.

88
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
[Neon] Don’t ask me. I have no idea.

89
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
But here, just ask daddy.

90
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,000
I’ve got his number
saved here in my phone.

91
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Squala. You make the call.

92
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
[gasps] Why do I have to?

93
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
You’re the most experienced
and we need a new leader.

94
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
-So, it should be you
-Oh no!

95
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
That’s completely out of the question!

96
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
I’m just not leader material.

97
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Then perhaps we should put it
to a vote to be fair.

98
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,000
We need to make the call
as soon as possible.

99
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
And my vote’s for Kurapika.

100
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
He’s the one who captured the bandit,

101
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
and he’s shown excellent judgment.

102
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,000
I believe he would make
the most effective leader.

103
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Works for me.

104
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,000
I vote for Kurapika, too.

105
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
That’s that.

106
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,000
So, you make the call.

107
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Very well.

108
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Then as interim leader,
I’ll call Mr. Nostrade.

109
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,000
But only...

110
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:24,000
until we can confirm
what’s really become of Dalzollene.

111
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Further choices will be made
by Mr. Nostrade.

112
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
I didn’t expect this to happen so soon…

113
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,000
It would be inappropriate for me to call.

114
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,000
So, would you please
provide an introduction?

115
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Okay.

116
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
[Neon] Here. I’m putting him on now.

117
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
[Kurapika] Hello?

118
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Is it true that Dalzollene
has been killed?

119
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,000
[Kurapika] Yes, sir.

120
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
That’s quite hard to believe.

121
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
He is a Nen user.

122
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:06,000
He’s trained to withstand ten gunshots
without sustaining any injuries.

123
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
He was killed by outlaws
known as the Phantom Troupe.

124
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Wait… The Spiders?

125
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,000
[Kurapika] I had the opportunity
to see them in action.

126
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,000
One of them stopped a bazooka round
with his bare hand.

127
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
My name is Kurapika
and I’m the interim leader.

128
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Can you please tell me
how you would like us to proceed?

129
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Of course.

130
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
But first I want to hear what you think.

131
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,000
[Kurapika] I believe your daughter

132
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
should leave
Yorknew City immediately, sir.

133
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:38,000
I’m not confident that we can protect her
in the event of unforeseen circumstances.

134
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:43,000
[Nostrade] I agree with your assessment,
but my daughter has a say, as well.

135
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
I want to respect her wishes
whenever possible.

136
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Her safety’s my top priority.

137
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Hmm...

138
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,000
Understood.

139
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
I’m on my way there right now,

140
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,000
so I should arrive
sometime tomorrow evening.

141
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:00,000
I promise I’ll do my best
to persuade Neon.

142
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,000
You will be the new leader, Kurapika.

143
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Here is your first order:

144
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Keep an eye on Neon until I get there.

145
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Yes, sir. I will.

146
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Your father wants you to know
he’ll be here tomorrow evening.

147
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Really? That’s perfect!

148
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
When he lands,
I’ll get him to take me shopping!

149
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Until then he made it quite clear
that he’d like you to stay in your room.

150
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,000
Aw...

151
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
I wanted to see the casino…

152
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
You stay here with the boss.

153
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
What?! Yeah, I got it.

154
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
I’ll be downstairs.

155
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
[gulping]

156
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
[refreshed exhale]

157
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,000
This is it!

158
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
It says here

159
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,000
that a dummy corporation
for the Nostrade family

160
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
owns that building you were in.

161
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
All right then, do you think
you can track down a list

162
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
of all the buildings
in this area the Nostrade family own?

163
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Sure can!

164
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,000
I can also see,

165
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
if anyone has checked into a hotel
using the Nostrade name lately.

166
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,000
[metal bang]

167
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Okay. I brought some more beer.

168
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Hey! Thanks a lot!

169
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Here ya go.

170
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Know what you need, Uvo?
A Hunter’s License.

171
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
As long as you have the money,

172
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
you can dig up
all kinds of information from their site.

173
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Unlike you guys,
I don’t like the idea of money.

174
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
If I want something, I take it.

175
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
[Shalnark] Well said!

176
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
-You’re an exemplary bandit.
-[Uvogin gulping]

177
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Here.

178
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,000
They own two other buildings
in Yorknew City.

179
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,000
And there are three hotels
where members are staying.

180
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
All right.
This search shouldn’t take too long.

181
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
There.

182
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,000
Thanks, buddy.

183
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,000
I owe ya one.

184
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,000
[loud smooch]

185
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Whoa! What are you doing?!

186
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:11,000
[chuckles] Well... I’m off.

187
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,000
[Franklin] What about the beer?

188
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
You guys can finish it.

189
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Make sure you dispose of the body.

190
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
And try to make it quick.

191
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Yeah.

192
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
-Later.
-Hey, Uvo!

193
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Huh?

194
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Don’t get careless out there.

195
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
No prob.

196
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Family members…

197
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Sounds like a good place to start.

198
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
[Kurapika] Look at this.

199
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,000
What’s that?

200
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:56,000
A list of the buildings the Nostrades own?

201
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
And a list of family members.

202
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
I didn’t know this was out there.

203
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
This website can only be accessed
by pro Hunters.

204
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,000
With this information,

205
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
they can find the location of this room
without any trouble at all.

206
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,000
There’s a website just for pro Hunters?

207
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
That means if one of our enemies
is a pro Hunter, too.

208
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,000
We’re in trouble.

209
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
We need to move the boss
to a different room right away.

210
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,000
[Melody] We do? In the same hotel?

211
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
It’s faster and cleaner that way.

212
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
But do not use aliases!

213
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
We’ll have Melody or Basho book the room.

214
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,000
And don’t let anyone leave,
especially the boss.

215
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
You got it.

216
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
[Kurapika]
Don’t check out of this one, either.

217
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Hold on. What about you?

218
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
[Kurapika] I'll stay here.

219
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Oh?!

220
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,000
Kurapika… You’re not thinking of...?

221
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
[man] I-- I don’t think
he’s a family member.

222
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
He’s a bodyguard for the boss’s daughter.

223
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,000
[Uvogin] His daughter?

224
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Yeah.

225
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:10,000
She’s a freak who gets her kicks
out of collecting body parts.

226
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,000
[grunts] Eyeballs, organs, guts…

227
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
Oh! And she’s a fortune teller!

228
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
She’s really accurate, too!

229
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,000
That so?

230
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Yeah! She’s got a long list
of clients in the Mafia.

231
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Some of the community elders
practically worship her!

232
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
[nervous chuckle]

233
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,000
[Uvogin] Oh?

234
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,000
I mean it makes sense.

235
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Our boss used his daughter’s power
to make his entire fortune.

236
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Look, cut me some slack, all right?

237
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,000
I told you everything I know,
so just let me--

238
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
[Uvogin] Someone who can see the future.

239
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,000
So, she knew this attack was gonna happen?

240
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,000
The boss was right.

241
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,000
There weren’t any traitors among us
after all.

242
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:05,000
[Leorio] As it stands, we have a diamond
worth three million jenny

243
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,000
and 2.4 million in leftover cash.

244
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,000
Not to mention the 2.75
we made arm wrestling.

245
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,000
All told that’s
a total of around eight million.

246
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
We need at least nine billion.

247
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
That’s the minimum opening bid
for Greed Island,

248
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,000
so if we don’t have that,
there’s really no point.

249
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:27,000
But I don’t see how we’re gonna get there.
Not through legitimate channels anyway.

250
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Yeah, I wouldn’t call
that kind of arm wrestling "legitimate."

251
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,000
All of the challengers toward the end

252
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
were a bunch of desperate losers
looking for revenge.

253
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
And that’s okay.

254
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
See, that was my goal
from the very beginning.

255
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
[Gon and Killua] Huh?

256
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
[Leorio] The more exaggerated the rumors,
the better.

257
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,000
What do you mean by that?

258
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
The arm wrestling was just bait.

259
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,000
[Gon] It was?

260
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,000
That is what’s gonna draw all the moles
out of hiding!

261
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Wait, moles?

262
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,000
I don’t think I get it.
Why do we want moles?

263
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
[Leorio] Okay, take it easy.

264
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Just let me explain…

265
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,000
[Gon and Killua] [uncertain grunt]

266
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
[Leorio] Step right up!

267
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Conditional auction!

268
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:09,000
We’ve got a diamond sitting here
that’s worth three million jenny!

269
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
Arm wrestling decides the winner!

270
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:15,000
The first person to beat this boy
wins the diamond.

271
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,000
The entry fee’s 10,000 jenny.

272
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,000
What? He’s just a kid!

273
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,000
I just might try it…

274
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,000
Don't bother.

275
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,000
That kid beat 500 people yesterday,
no problem.

276
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
[man] Really?

277
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Yeah, really, and more than 20 of ‘em
got their arms broken.

278
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,000
Seriously?

279
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:38,000
[Leorio] [chuckles] The rumors
are starting to spread nicely.

280
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Well, in that case…

281
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Outta my way.

282
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Oh! Do we have our first challenger?

283
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,000
[short man] Not quite.

284
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,000
[gasps]

285
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
[short man]
I already know my man can’t beat your kid.

286
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,000
I was watching yesterday.

287
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
[Leorio] Then what do you want?

288
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
You interested in makin’ some real money?

289
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
What do you mean?

290
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,000
I know where you can make serious cash.

291
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Not the measly pocket change
you’re pulling here.

292
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
You can make hundreds...

293
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:10,000
no, thousands of times more, easy.

294
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
[chuckling]

295
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
So, are these two the moles?

296
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,000
Yeah. It looks like
we just landed a big fish!

297
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Fish? So... they’re not moles?

298
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Will you please stop talking?
It doesn’t matter!

299
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,000
[short man] Here we are.

300
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,000
[elevator dings]

301
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,000
[straining]

302
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,000
[grunting]

303
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
[cheering]

304
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,000
[Killua] Oh, wow.

305
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
I can feel the bloodlust.

306
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,000
This competition accepts all comers,
and it really pays out.

307
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
The spectators bet on each match

308
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:10,000
and the winner gets ten percent
of all bets placed.

309
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,000
We’re talking billions
wagered on each match.

310
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,000
But that means every single win
could make you millions!

311
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
More if you play your cards right.

312
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
I get a commission

313
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
but it’s only 50 percent
of whatever you earn.

314
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:25,000
Fifty? Isn’t that a bit steep?

315
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,000
If I don’t enter your name,
you can’t participate.

316
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Besides you can bet your own money.

317
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
That kid’ll get great odds,

318
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
so you’ll make it back
a hundred times over.

319
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
Okay, I’m sold!

320
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,000
We’re in! Gon! Do it!

321
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Huh?

322
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
[referee]
Well? Do we have any other challengers?

323
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,000
[short man] Right over here!

324
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
This kid thinks he’s got what it takes.

325
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
All right!

326
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,000
[gasping]

327
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Sorry to disappoint you, folks!

328
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:03,000
But the arm wrestling
has officially been canceled!

329
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Instead, we’re gonna do
a little bit of conditional auctioning!

330
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,000
[upset crowd]

331
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,000
What’s wrong? Why’s it canceled?

332
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
I, uh... I don’t actually know…

333
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
And all you have to do to win is...

334
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,000
play a game of hide-and-seek!

335
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Hide-and-seek? Really?

336
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,000
[punk] We’ll start by passing out flyers!

337
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:27,000
Now take a good look
at those pictures, folks!

338
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Don’t forget ‘em,

339
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:32,000
because the seven guys and gals you see
are your targets!

340
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Hey… I’ve seen that girl with the glasses.

341
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Me too. She arm-wrestled me.

342
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,000
[man] Wait…

343
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,000
You think they’re the ones responsible
for what happened last night?

344
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Yeah. You mean the attack
on the auction, right?

345
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,000
[gasps]

346
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
[punk] In order to win the bid,

347
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:54,000
all you have to do is capture a target
and deliver them to us.

348
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,000
For each, you’ll walk away

349
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,000
with the tidy sum of…

350
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:00,000
wait for it… two billion jenny!

351
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
[crowd gasping]

352
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,000
[punk] There is no time limit.

353
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,000
And it doesn’t matter
if they’re dead or alive!

354
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Interested? Then catch one and call us!

355
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,000
Two billion each is a lot!

356
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,000
And if we catch all seven,
that’s 14 billion!

357
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:20,000
[punk] All it costs to participate
is a mere five million jenny!

358
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,000
We’re participating, right?

359
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,000
[Gon] Sure…

360
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,000
[participant 1] That’s right.

361
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
I’ll fax you the information.

362
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
[participant 2] Check the website.

363
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
We’ll pay for anything concrete.

364
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,000
[Leorio] We’re gonna need to hurry.

365
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,000
[Killua] No rush.

366
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,000
They won’t be able to catch our targets.

367
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,000
[Leorio and Gon] Huh?

368
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
Even the Mafia’s having
a hard time with them.

369
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,000
What do you mean?

370
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,000
The "conditional auction"
they’re having?

371
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,000
It’s nothing more than a big bounty hunt.

372
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
It’s like...

373
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,000
the Mafia’s admitting
they can’t catch these targets.

374
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Or not alone, anyway.

375
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
You’ve got a point there.

376
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
They were willing to put
everything else on hold

377
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
just so they could track them down...

378
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:12,000
I heard, last night, someone
attacked the underground auction.

379
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
But who would do that?!

380
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,000
Unless… maybe it was them.

381
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:20,000
You think that’s the reason
they’ve got a bounty on their heads?

382
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Yup.

383
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,000
And if they stole from the Mafia,
they’ve got a screw loose.

384
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,000
But think.

385
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,000
Who do we know
that’s crazy enough to do that?

386
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,000
The Phantom Troupe!

387
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Now that you mention it,

388
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
what’s Kurapika been up to?

389
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Dunno. He should be here
in the city by now

390
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,000
but he hasn’t called yet.

391
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Then I’ll call him.

392
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
[phone rings]

393
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
[phone continues ringing]

394
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
He's not answering.

395
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Maybe he’s working…

396
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,000
Working?

397
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Yeah, I heard he picked up a job
as a bodyguard a while back.

398
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:24,000
I bet it’s some big shot VIP.

399
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:28,000
He’s looking for the Scarlet Eyes,
so probably someone in the underworld.

400
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,000
What if he was guarding them
at the auction hall

401
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
and then got caught up in the attack?

402
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,000
He wouldn’t have let
something like that happen.

403
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,000
If the Troupe attacked,

404
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Kurapika would be tracking them down
even as we speak.

405
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:44,000
I wouldn’t be surprised,
if he’s captured a few of ‘em already.

406
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
I hope you're right.

407
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,000
[ringing tone]

408
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,000
[phone ringing]

409
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[clatter]

410
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
You by yourself?

411
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,000
That’s pretty impressive.

412
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Where do you want to die?

413
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,000
I’ll let you decide the location.

414
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:25,000
I’d prefer somewhere remote,
so we won’t be a nuisance.

415
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
I don’t want your screams
to bother anyone.

416
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,000
[angry grunt]

417
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:35,000
[narrator] Uvogin has come
to get revenge for his capture

418
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:38,000
and restore his wounded pride.

419
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:41,000
And Kurapika has long awaited the chance

420
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:44,000
to exact revenge upon the Phantom Troupe.

421
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Their battle is about to begin.

422
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
[theme song playing]

423
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,000
[Gon] Coming up:

424
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

425
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:01,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

426
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

427
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

428
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Today, we're introducing Squala,
one of Neon’s guards.

429
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:10,000
A Manipulator who controls dogs
using his Nen.

430
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,000
And he’s actually dating Neon’s maid,
Miss Eliza.

431
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:14,000
-Meow, meow!
-Woof, woof!

432
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:20,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Condition x and x Condition."

433
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,000
Explain the difference
using 30 words or less!

434
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Killua] A condition is a rule,

435
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
and a condition’s a covenant
with yourself!
